00:02:33.395 --> 00:02:41.585
English, French, and Japanese and Chinese,
so I have very rarely written in Japanese.

00:02:42.005 --> 00:02:48.065
But I have written a lot in French
and Chinese, and in both cases

00:02:48.065 --> 00:02:52.985
I wrote by hand because in those
days there were no other options.

00:02:53.075 --> 00:02:55.595
I wrote my Chinese by hand and I wrote...

00:02:55.745 --> 00:02:57.215
I was a student in France for three years.

00:02:57.215 --> 00:02:59.645
I had to write, you know, exams in French.

00:02:59.675 --> 00:03:01.655
I wrote by hand in Chinese.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.985
Uh, after one year of study, we
had to write the, I had to write

00:03:04.985 --> 00:03:06.485
the British Foreign Service Exam.

00:03:06.845 --> 00:03:09.485
I had to compose a
diplomatic note in Chinese.

00:03:09.905 --> 00:03:15.740
I had to translate uh, newspaper
editorials from English into Chinese.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:19.670
I had to be able to write, and so I
did a lot of writing and I'm quite

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:25.010
convinced that writing by hand
helped me learn Chinese characters.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:30.980
If I were learning Chinese characters
today, would I write them all by hand,

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.735
uh, out by hand, as I did then or
would I rely on some computer system?

00:03:35.735 --> 00:03:39.335
I don't know because I'm not in the
position of having to learn Chinese

00:03:39.335 --> 00:03:41.345
characters today, 50 years later.

00:03:42.035 --> 00:03:46.745
But I'm quite convinced that writing
them out by hand helps me learn them.

00:03:48.035 --> 00:03:53.165
Yet I know that I rarely, if I,
I do not write by hand in any

00:03:53.575 --> 00:03:54.845
language other than English today.

00:03:54.905 --> 00:03:59.375
I write, I can write Chinese,
Japanese, Russian, whatever.

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:03.875
I will either type or I will
use dictation on my iPhone.

00:04:04.235 --> 00:04:05.645
I don't write by hand.

00:04:06.035 --> 00:04:11.555
Uh, in Russian I can hardly read the
cursive version of the Cyrillic alphabet.

00:04:12.065 --> 00:04:14.315
Uh, basically everything
I do is on the computer.

00:04:14.345 --> 00:04:15.635
That's the world that I live in.

00:04:15.905 --> 00:04:21.334
So if I were even today, I, I, I have
never tried to write Persian or Arabic.

00:04:22.465 --> 00:04:26.546
So, uh, as I said, I don't write
very much in the languages that

00:04:26.551 --> 00:04:29.635
I have learned or I type on the
computer, but I don't write by hand.

00:04:30.055 --> 00:04:33.895
But writing is a great way to improve
your skills in the language, your

00:04:33.895 --> 00:04:38.505
comprehension, but particularly your
ability to output to speak 'cause

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:41.995
you look words up, so it's kind of
like an assist to get to speaking.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:46.159
Well, I'm gonna show you an
even further, more helpful

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.289
