00:09:40.745 --> 00:09:45.425
I hope that was useful, but if I really
wanted to improve in those languages,

00:09:46.215 --> 00:09:47.435
probably I should write by hand.

00:09:47.705 --> 00:09:52.430
And there is research that shows that
not only for learning languages, but for

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:57.950
learning anything if we write by hand and
we're cultivating those motor skills in

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:03.950
our brain to enable us to write and to
to write about a subject or to write in a

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:10.550
language that we are learning, doing it by
hand is more effective than typing, more

00:10:10.555 --> 00:10:12.270
effective than just listening and reading.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:17.345
So I, I'm quite convinced that there
is significant benefit in writing by

00:10:17.345 --> 00:10:19.835
hand in order to improve our skills.

00:10:20.015 --> 00:10:23.165
But it's also a matter of say, choice.

00:10:23.555 --> 00:10:29.345
If I spend a lot of time writing
by hand, then that's time that I'm

00:10:29.345 --> 00:10:31.235
not spending listening and reading.

00:10:31.415 --> 00:10:34.895
So my, the, my vocabulary
growth is more limited.

00:10:35.375 --> 00:10:39.695
Uh, it's a, it's kind of the, the way I
feel when I'm say on LingQ and I'm doing

00:10:39.695 --> 00:10:42.710
sort of vocabulary in sentence mode.

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:47.660
We have these matching pairs now
in the, uh, certainly the iOS app,

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:50.840
followed by the sort of assembling
of words in a sentence, which I love

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.430
doing and I find very addictive.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:56.560
But all the time I'm spending doing
that and nailing those things down.

00:10:57.755 --> 00:11:03.005
That's time that I'm not acquiring more
words and getting my brain used to hearing

00:11:03.005 --> 00:11:04.715
the language and reading the language.

00:11:04.715 --> 00:11:07.655
So there's, it's always a
matter of, of what you wanna do.

00:11:07.985 --> 00:11:10.895
Obviously when I was learning
Chinese, it was a full-time job.

00:11:10.895 --> 00:11:13.385
I had the whole day to
devote to learning Chinese.

00:11:13.625 --> 00:11:16.325
I could spend an hour or two
writing, I could spend an hour

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.555
or two listening or reading.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:23.250
So there was, I, I didn't have to decide
as I do today, how am I gonna spend

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:26.850
the hour, hour and a half a day that I
have available for language learning?

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:31.170
However, if you have the time, I'm
quite convinced that writing by

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:36.270
hand is a very good discipline, uh,
to improve your language skills.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:40.910
But overall, I think writing it's
something that's perhaps neglected today

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:45.260
and, and maybe is really only necessary
if we are in a, a situation where we need

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:49.040
to be able to write in a foreign language
for academic or professional reasons.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:55.070
And then, uh, you can refer to the videos
that I did on writing to see what my

00:11:55.075 --> 00:11:59.690
recommendations are with regard to, you
know, how to improve your writing, but

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.820
insofar as writing by hand is concerned...

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:05.360
oh, and that reminds me when I did
my video about writing and I said

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:09.770
that, you know, keeping a diary is
not something that I would do because

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:11.330
it's not something I'm used to doing.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:17.630
Somebody commented that somehow, uh, I
was misleading people, uh, and that I saw,

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:21.440
you know, the writing practice, uh, or
the writing of a maintaining of a diary.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:26.480
It wasn't clear what the reference was
to, but that I saw this as competition

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:30.080
to LingQ and that therefore I was
discouraging people from doing it.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:31.820
That's not the case.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:37.985
No learning activity, let's say a learning
activity that is totally unrelated

00:12:37.985 --> 00:12:40.195
to LingQ is a competition to LingQ.

00:12:40.895 --> 00:12:44.075
Different learning activities
are all complimentary.

00:12:45.035 --> 00:12:49.115
You don't have to only have one
learning activity, one learning app,

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.675
one approach to language learning.

00:12:50.675 --> 00:12:54.365
Whatever you do, uh, is beneficial.

00:12:54.935 --> 00:12:58.355
Uh, remember, language learning is
a matter of your attitude and the

00:12:58.355 --> 00:13:00.335
time you spend with the language.

00:13:01.025 --> 00:13:04.430
Whatever gets you involved
with the language is good.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:05.810
That's not competition.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.750
That's basically synergy
from my point of view.

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:14.690
So again, I refer you to the two videos
I did on writing or a few years ago, and

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:16.490
I hope that this is of interest to you.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:17.420
Thanks for listening.

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:18.390
Bye for now.

